  "reading": "a = mixed, b = oracle_hop_matched throughout. On the deployable unguided prompting condition, hop-matched retrieval (oracle) moves hop_count_exact_match significantly (McNemar p=0.0006, paired t p=0.00048; mixed 0.515 vs oracle 0.600, +0.085) but does NOT move step_f1 or ordered_step_accuracy (both CIs straddle zero, both t-tests not significant; point estimates nearly tied, mixed marginally ahead on step_f1 0.2035 vs 0.1931). composite_score's apparent oracle-favouring gap (+0.053 in b's favour) is not trustworthy per the composite_score_caveat -- oracle's reference_validity_micro jumps from 0.0 to 0.278, which per issue #40's analysis is a regex/bracket-vs-bare-# artifact, not a measured decomposition-quality effect. This mirrors exp-004's within-model finding on the guided/unguided axis: an oracle signal helps get the step COUNT right more often without a measured step-QUALITY gain. Router-hop-matched (the third ADR 0022 condition) remains unmeasurable -- today's router writes no query id (ADR 0022 item 5) -- so the oracle-minus-router error-propagation number is NOT estimated here and is not present in this file."
